---
# Unlike docker.yaml (never provided on the Docker side either), this file has to exist here
# specifically because of how the gethomepage image behaves: servicesFromKubernetes() calls
# checkAndCopyConfig("kubernetes.yaml") on EVERY service/widget lookup (service-helpers.js,
# via getServiceItem's docker/kubernetes discovery fallback — unconditional, not gated on any
# service actually using a kubernetes: widget). checkAndCopyConfig only copies its skeleton
# when the file is missing; against this role's read-only Secret mount at /app/config that
# copy fails with EROFS and the app calls process.exit(1) — a crash loop on the very first
# widget poll. Pre-supplying an empty file here (parses to undefined; config?.mode is then
# undefined, getKubeConfig() falls through to `default: return null`) avoids the write
# entirely. No kubernetes-widget usage is configured, so `mode` stays unset on purpose.
